    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57dbc3c5_890f9008",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1087,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-17T04:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m thinking we should probably do straightforward rejection checks like this in the HC itself.  They\u0027re relatively simple, can be performed outside the task, and then the kernel gets an immediate failure rather than a delayed one from a notification",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1087,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1087,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9665de0_27c7902d",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1087,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-18T16:44:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we do that, then I would want the checks to be done through API calls into pe_ functions and those function clearly indicate they are running on another tasks so can only access things in an atomic way",
      "parentUuid": "57dbc3c5_890f9008",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1087,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1087,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3764fa44_1bf78146",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1087,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-18T16:49:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds reasonable",
      "parentUuid": "a9665de0_27c7902d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1087,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1087,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79d609f0_c876912a",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1087,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T06:02:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I used an accessor, but that accessor doesn\u0027t take any explicit synchronization actions. Neither do any of the other simple getters I looked at in usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c. Is that a problem?\n\nFurthermore, note that some SVDMs may be sent by the UFP. If we wanted to support passing through, e.g. Discover Modes from the host, we would have to inspect the VDM header when we do this check. Do we care about this use case? If so, is that too low-level for the host command to concern itself with, or would you still want to handle it there?",
      "parentUuid": "3764fa44_1bf78146",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1087,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1087,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c7c8378_a902bd18",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1087,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T20:31:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are we talking atomic gets/sets of the data role, Jett?  I think I\u0027d assumed that the atomic ops were most needed when they\u0027re variables we\u0027re read/modify/writing like the flags. \n\nI suspect it would be reasonable to have the host command perform the level of checks we do in pe_can_send_sop_vdm() currently (and possibly make that a generally accessible pd_* function if we\u0027re safe running from another task)",
      "parentUuid": "79d609f0_c876912a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1087,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1087,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "147251a2_f91af7c5",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1087,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-20T18:10:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we do any checking in the host command task (to let the AP know more quickly of a failure), I would still want to perform those same checks on the PD task since it is very possible that the state has changed since then - since the PD task is the controller of the state.\n\nI don\u0027t know how much value there is in telling the AP 200ms sooner that the request was bad or not (for more complex state checking). Either way, the PD task defintely needs to verify that the state is still appropriate before proceeding (so we should add this DRP check back into the PD task as well)\n\nAnything that the host command access should probably go through pd_* function and though functions should clearly indicate that they are called from other tasks. Those function should only be reading a state or setting flags atomically - nothing more.\n\nto me pd_ prefix is the API interface of the pd framework to other modules/code/tasks and we should know that pd_ means they need to be thread/task safe.",
      "parentUuid": "0c7c8378_a902bd18",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1087,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1087,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e5cede6_1f02c48b",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1087,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-20T20:49:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "True, our data role could have changed.  So we could consolidate checks into the PD task and count on notifications to the AP to let them know what\u0027s up.  I can check with Prashant on his thoughts there. \n\nAgreed that pd_* functions should be used for any host command checks.",
      "parentUuid": "147251a2_f91af7c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1087,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1087,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f06a2da_61e180a2",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1087,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-01T01:32:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the concerns about when to check things aren\u0027t very relevant until the host command makes it back in. It looks like I removed this check in Patchset 3 for reasons that currently escape me. I added it back in in `dpm_attempt_mode_entry`, next to the other checks.",
      "parentUuid": "1e5cede6_1f02c48b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1087,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1087,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3a786be_bbc81267",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1093,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-17T04:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Long-ish run we\u0027ll have to revisit the idea of whether we want to keep the flag for discover being done, and when to set it.  It saves us running through our full discovery checklist every ready run, but is also redundant information. \n\nIt might also be worth breaking into SOP done and SOP\u0027 done when we do notifications, since we could potentially end up with a partner which won\u0027t allow us to discover one or the other (ex. if we can\u0027t swap to vconn source), but the kernel would still be capable of acting on the info we did collect (really, entering DP most likely).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1093,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 1093,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "708bf9bb_de355dc2",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1093,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-18T16:44:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 to separating SOP\u0027 and SOP notifications",
      "parentUuid": "d3a786be_bbc81267",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1093,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 1093,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe33941_b328538f",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1093,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T06:02:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WRT redundancy, I intend that vdm_cmd should die with pe_do_port_discovery. As it stands, this flag really means, \"DP setup done,\" so it has the wrong name. My expectation is that the EC would generate a notification for each host command/SVDM ACK in the mode entry/setup sequence. If that included SOP\u0027, e.g. USB4, then there would be SOP\u0027-specific notifications.\n\nBut it sounds like you\u0027re talking about notifications for when we\u0027ve finished actual discovery. It probably does make sense to separate notifications for SOP and SOP\u0027. I could also imagine a single notification that just says \"discovery updated,\" and we would send it whenever we had discovered as much as we could and then subsequently when we discovered anything else. That might be more trouble than its worth, though.",
      "parentUuid": "708bf9bb_de355dc2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1093,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 1093,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "001a1855_47665182",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1368,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-17T04:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve been half contemplating a new config, which you\u0027d set in development and disable once the kernel is ready enough to enter modes.  What are your thoughts?  It occurs to me that platforms coming up a couple of years from now might be able to enter modes via the kernel early in bring up, they wouldn\u0027t need the EC DPM long.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1366,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1368,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74109811_5242ceb9",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1368,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T06:02:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That seems reasonable to me. If there is a direct connection between being unlocked and driving DP, it is not obvious to me. Do you think I should do that as part of this CL?\n\nOr should I wait to do any such gating until the AP is actually capable of setting up DP?",
      "parentUuid": "001a1855_47665182",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1366,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1368,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93cd5a25_5e1c9f6c",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1368,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T20:31:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can pick a config to gate with later on.  It might have to be one that honeybuns will use to drive its DFP port as well.  I need to spend some quality time updating the API doc this week.",
