    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6feafd87_7d817038",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 6547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-17T04:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When passing in parameters for the command (ex. the VDM bits) I\u0027m guessing we\u0027ll want to create a union to hold the command arguments.  If we make it a decent size, then we should hopefully be able to keep supporting new sub-commands on the same version HC",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6544,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6547,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb7fea41_c14a3755",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 6547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T06:02:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we reasonably assume that any figure subcommand will use a port number, and thus port should be outside the union?\n\nCan you elaborate on \"make it a decent size\"? By default, it will be whatever size the largest parameter pack in the union is. I\u0027m assuming you\u0027re considering the scenario where the AP supports a subcommand that the EC doesn\u0027t. If the AP sends it using a newer, larger union definition, the EC should just slice the union when it accesses it, right? But it would reject the command for having an unknown subcommand anyway, before it tried to access the union, right?",
      "parentUuid": "6feafd87_7d817038",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6544,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6547,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffecfdff_d362ecd1",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 6547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T20:31:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, port should be outside the union.\n\nIf I remember correctly, changing the size of the command means we\u0027d need to up-version it (thought Jett can probably provide better details there).  So if we need to expand the command size, we need a new structure in addition to the old structure and code needs to work on both. \n But if we leave space in the union using a reserved field, we can keep using the same size command with new sub-commands in the future that need more space.  We\u0027ll still reject unknown sub-commands, but it should hopefully save us some structure bookkeeping.",
      "parentUuid": "bb7fea41_c14a3755",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6544,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6547,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "0357f1b2d4c059795f86baca4ac5d9526bde16ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
